---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { buildSEOMeta, getHubUrl } from '../../../lib/seoEngine';

const lang = 'en';
const title = 'Work Hours Calculation Guide 2025';
const description = 'Learn how to calculate your work hours accurately, deduct breaks, and maintain a precise timesheet for payroll and billing.';

const seo = buildSEOMeta(
  'hub',
  lang,
  {},
  '/en/guides/how-to-calculate-work-hours/',
  'de',
  '/ratgeber/arbeitszeit-berechnen/'
);

const hubUrl = getHubUrl(lang);
---

<BaseLayout 
  title={seo.title}
  description={seo.description}
  canonical={seo.canonical}
  hreflang={seo.hreflang}
  lang={lang}
>
  <article class="guide-content">
    <header class="guide-header">
      <nav class="breadcrumb">
        <a href={hubUrl}>Home</a> › <a href="/en/guides/">Guides</a> › Work Hours Calculation
      </nav>
      <h1>{title}</h1>
      <p class="lead">Accurate work hour calculation ensures fair pay, legal compliance, and effective project management. This guide covers the essential math for every professional.</p>
    </header>

    <div class="glass-card content-card">
      <section>
        <h2>1. Gross vs. Net Work Hours</h2>
        <p><strong>Gross work hours</strong> represent the total time from start to finish. <strong>Net work hours</strong> are the actual productive hours after subtracting breaks.</p>
        <div class="formula">
          <code>Net Hours = (End Time - Start Time) - Total Break Duration</code>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>2. Standard Work Break Rules</h2>
        <p>While laws vary by region, most countries have minimum break requirements:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Over 6 hours:</strong> Minimum 30 minutes.</li>
          <li><strong>Over 8 hours:</strong> Minimum 45 to 60 minutes.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Maintaining these breaks isn't just a legal requirement — it's vital for maintaining productivity and reducing burnout.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>3. Calculating Overtime</h2>
        <p>Overtime occurs when daily or weekly contracted hours are exceeded. To track it, you must first establish your baseline hours per period.</p>
        <a href={hubUrl} class="btn btn-primary">Start Calculating Hours Now</a>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>4. Why Automated Calculation Wins</h2>
        <p>Manual tracking is prone to rounding errors. Digital tools like <a href={hubUrl}>Time Calculator</a> provide instant decimal conversions (e.g., 8 hours 15 minutes = 8.25 hours), which are essential for billing and payroll integrity.</p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .guide-content {
    max-width: 800px;
    margin: 2rem auto;
    padding: 0 1rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }
  .guide-header {
    margin-bottom: 3rem;
    text-align: center;
  }
  .breadcrumb {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }
  .breadcrumb a {
    color: var(--primary);
    text-decoration: none;
  }
  .lead {
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }
  h1 {
    font-size: 2.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    background: var(--grad-primary);
    -webkit-background-clip: text;
    -webkit-text-fill-color: transparent;
  }
  h2 {
    color: var(--primary);
    margin-top: 2rem;
  }
  .content-card {
    padding: 2.5rem;
  }
  .formula {
    background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.3);
    padding: 1rem;
    border-radius: 8px;
    margin: 1rem 0;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    border-left: 4px solid var(--primary);
  }
  ul {
    padding-left: 1.5rem;
    margin: 1rem 0;
  }
  li {
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }
  .btn {
    display: inline-block;
    margin-top: 2rem;
    padding: 1rem 2rem;
    background: var(--grad-primary);
    color: white;
    text-decoration: none;
    border-radius: 8px;
    font-weight: 600;
  }
</style>
